    Correctly respect "Vary" attributes when retrieving from cache

    Since Qt's network cache is entirely built around URL matches
    alone, add some downstream logic so that we correctly handle
    responses with a "Vary" attribute and ensure that we do
    not retrieve non-matching cached responses when the corresponding
    header value differs.

    Refs qgis#63009

    (cherry picked from commit 7d0977d2f2437f917cc49789c5930cea1283345e)

Nyall Dawson <nyall.dawson@gmail.com>	2026-03-04

    Don't allow multiple requests to attempt to write to same network cache resource

    Because QNetworkDiskCache filenames are built ENTIRELY off the request
    URL alone, we potentially may hit situations where multiple requests
    to the same url (eg from different threads) are attempting to save
    their responses to the same network cache file.

    Put a guard in place so that only the first ongoing request to
    that URL is permitted to save the result in the cache.

    (cherry picked from commit 2a5ae88f0f436591838a14c9ebd3f33e5ebf14e2)

