    qgsogrutils: Fix ogrGeometryToQgsGeometry for 3d/m wkb case

    `OGR_G_ExportToWkb` returns wkb types with bit 31 set to 1 for 3d
    geometries. However, QGIS uses the OGC/ISO standard which uses the
    `+1000` encoding for 3d types.

    This issue can be reproduced when import 3d polyhedralsurface for
    example.
    This is fixed by using `OGR_G_ExportToIsoWkb` instead.

