Jean Felder <jean.felder@oslandia.com>	2025-04-09

    qgsgeos: Handle GEOS 3.13 change of NaN points in QgsGeos::fromGeos

    Since GEOS 3.13, Points with NaN coordinates are not considered empty
    anymore. Therefore, `GEOSisEmpty_r` will not return true if the input
    GeosGeometry contains NaN coordinates.

    This change is handled by checking if the generated QgsPoint is
    empty. If that's the case, a `nullptr` is returned to preserve QGIS to
    backward compatibility.

    See: https://github.com/libgeos/geos/pull/927

