Nyall Dawson <nyall.dawson@gmail.com>	2025-03-13

    [mssql] When validating query layers, ensuring we can run aggregate queries

    Eg check that we can run the geometry type check query. Some queries
    will happily run as top-level queries on SQL Server, but throw
    exceptions when they are subqueries.

    An example would be

    SELECT TOP 10 * FROM [table] where [a_string_col] = 24

    This query can execute as a standalone, but as soon as its part
    of a subquery SQL server will raise an exception due to the
    string/int casting.

    Now we catch these issues in validation and show the exception
    message from SQL server to the user, so that they can fix their
    query.

