Jean Felder <jean.felder@oslandia.com>	2024-06-23

    qgs3daxis: Fix cube face picking

    When clicking on a face of the cube, the view is rotated according
    to the clicked face. However, this needs `TrianglePicking` to be
    enabled to properly detect the face because it needs the
    `primitiveIndex` of the hit. `TrianglePicking` was activated
    by default up to commit b371267fbe117ecf54f56dd8c9948db0d89dfdd1 which
    restored it to the default picking method: `BoundingVolumePicking`.

    This issue is fixed by enabling `TrianglePicking` when entering the
    viewport if the cube is visible. `TrianglePicking` is then deactivated
    when leaving the viewport.

    Fixes: commit b371267fbe117ecf54f56dd8c9948db0d89dfdd1

